<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela sells U.S. insurance firm for $2.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Venezuela sells U.S. insurance firm for $2.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's state Deposits Guarantee Fund (Fogade) sold Florida-based insurance company Consolidated Property and Casualty Insurance Company to U.S. company North Pointe Financial Service Inc for $2.501 million, Fogade officials said.</p>
<p>North Pointe was the only bidder at the auction for which a $2.5 million base price had been set.</p>
<p>Consolidated passed to Fogade in 1994 as part of guarantees given by Venezuelan bank Banco Consolidado for financial aid during a severe financial sector crisis.</p>
<p>Consolidated had assets of $8.5 million and a net worth of $2.5 million at the end of 1996, Fogade said.</p>
<p>((-- Humberto Escobar, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
